---
/**
 * Method.astro — Phase 3
 *
 * Layout: editorial step list, dark section (depth mode per doc 11).
 * Four steps maximum — per brief. Process feels inevitable.
 *
 * Step numbering: Geist Mono (technical register, doc 11 Part 6).
 * Step names: Neue Haas Grotesk Display (structural register).
 * Step copy: Neue Haas Grotesk Text (body register).
 *
 * The step numbers earn their place: the method IS a sequence.
 * Order carries information the reader needs. This is the exception
 * to taste-skill's numbering caution — not section markers, process steps.
 *
 * Label rule (doc 11, Rule 6): label above every headline.
 * Rule 4 (doc 11): no centered headlines on dark sections. Flush left.
 *
 * Isotipo (doc 11, Part 5): structural background presence at bottom-right.
 * On dark surface: opacity only, no blend mode — white areas contribute
 * barely-perceptible brightness at 5% opacity (below the "visible" threshold).
 *
 * data-reveal: intentionally omitted in Phase 3.
 * Phase 4 adds IntersectionObserver — attributes added then.
 */
---

<section class="method section section-dark" id="metodo" aria-label="Método">

  <!-- Isotipo — bottom-right structural mark on dark section -->
  <div class="method-isotipo" aria-hidden="true">
    <img
      src="/images/isotipo.png"
      alt=""
      width="600"
      height="600"
      draggable="false"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="container method-container">

    <!-- Section header — label above headline per Rule 6 -->
    <header class="method-header">
      <p class="text-label method-lbl">Método</p>
      <h2 class="method-headline">Cómo funciona.</h2>
      <p class="method-intro">
        No empezamos con diseños. Empezamos por entender cómo opera tu negocio.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Steps — ordered list: sequence matters, order carries information -->
    <ol class="method-steps" role="list">

      <li class="method-step">
        <span class="step-num text-mono" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3 class="step-name">Entendemos</h3>
          <p class="step-body">
            Antes de diseñar, preguntamos. ¿Dónde se pierden los clientes? ¿Qué tarea se repite más? ¿Qué herramientas ya tienes y cuáles no están conectadas?
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="method-step">
        <span class="step-num text-mono" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3 class="step-name">Diseñamos</h3>
          <p class="step-body">
            Diseñamos el sistema completo antes de escribir código. El sitio, las automatizaciones, las integraciones: todo conectado desde el principio.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="method-step">
        <span class="step-num text-mono" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3 class="step-name">Construimos</h3>
          <p class="step-body">
            Construimos el sitio y todo lo que lo conecta a tu operación. No entregamos piezas sueltas, entregamos el sistema completo.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="method-step">
        <span class="step-num text-mono" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3 class="step-name">Verificamos</h3>
          <p class="step-body">
            El sistema funciona antes de que lo llamemos terminado. Probamos cada flujo, cada integración, cada punto de contacto con el cliente.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

    </ol>

  </div>

</section>

<style>
  /* ── Section ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .method {
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ── Isotipo ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /*
   * Override: .section-dark > * applies position:relative; z-index:1
   * globally. Astro's scoped attribute increases specificity of this
   * rule, so position:absolute and z-index:0 win here.
   *
   * z-index:0 places the isotipo behind content (z-index:1) but
   * above the noise grain pseudo-element (also z-index:0, but
   * ::after renders after regular elements, so grain is on top —
   * acceptable since grain is at 3.5% opacity and essentially invisible).
   */

  .method-isotipo {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: -6%;
    right: -5%;
    width: clamp(260px, 32vw, 480px);
    opacity: 0.05;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  .method-isotipo img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* ── Container ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /*
   * Explicit z-index:1 ensures content sits above noise grain
   * and the isotipo background mark.
   */

  .method-container {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  /* ── Header ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .method-header {
    max-width: 580px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }

  .method-lbl {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    color: var(--color-grey-dim-dark);
  }

  /* Item 7 (doc 11): 20–24px gap between label and headline */

  .method-headline {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 1.2rem + 4.5vw, 5.5rem);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    color: var(--color-cream);
  }

  .method-intro {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-grey-mid-dark);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 480px;
  }

  /* ── Steps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .method-steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  /* ── Step row ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /*
   * Grid: [step number fixed] [step content fills remaining width]
   * Step number: Geist Mono, muted, technical register.
   * This column stays at 56px on desktop — number is a coordinate,
   * not a headline. It should not compete with the step name.
   */

  .method-step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 56px 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    padding-block: var(--space-10);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-dark);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .step-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-regular);
    color: var(--color-grey-dim-dark);
    line-height: 1;
    padding-top: 5px;
    /* optical alignment with first line of step-name */
  }

  .step-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-snug);
    color: var(--color-cream);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .step-body {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-grey-mid-dark);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  /* ── Mobile — 768px and below ───────────────────────────────── */
  /*
   * Narrower number column, tighter gap.
   * Step content remains full-width — reads well single-column.
   */

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .method-step {
      grid-template-columns: 40px 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-5);
      padding-block: var(--space-8);
    }

    .method-isotipo {
      width: 68vw;
      bottom: -4%;
      right: -18%;
      opacity: 0.04;
    }

    .method-intro {
      max-width: 100%;
    }
  }

  /* ── Small mobile ───────────────────────────────────────────── */

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .method-isotipo {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
